# the COFF object model to and from the neutral object
#
# to_neutral reads a COFF object, regular or bigobj, into a neutral object
# through the naming rows, the relocation set of its machine and the facts
# below. what the neutral model has no field for travels in the object's
# facts, keyed by COFF, so nothing a file states is dropped and the
# conversion back gives a file that converts to the same neutral object. a
# header the conversion cannot carry, as COFF line numbers, an auxiliary
# record of a function definition, a block or a CLR token, a virtual size
# or address in an object, a bigobj header field other than the one every
# bigobj is written with, or a symbol or type in the record that counts a
# section's relocations, is refused rather than dropped.
#
# every section but .drectve and the mink note section is a neutral section of
# its name, its kind as the classifier reads its characteristics and name, its
# flags the memory characteristics state, and its alignment the ALIGN field's,
# sixteen when it states none as the PE Format default has it. a section of
# uninitialized data is zero fill. the characteristics the conversion back
# does not derive from the kind, flags and alignment are a fact. the .drectve
# options are the object's directives, and the constant-time ranges are
# decoded from the mink note section and its relocations, as coff/neutral/mark
# places them. a section of IMAGE_SCN_LNK_COMDAT is a group of its own: its
# section definition's selection names the rule, the first symbol defined in
# it after the definition names the signature and takes the section's size as
# its own, and an associative section's group follows the section its
# definition names, which it depends on. garbage collection treats each
# section as lld-link does, a COMDAT section kept when referenced, an
# associative one living with its leader and every other section a root,
# except unwind data outside a group, which lld-link keeps and the link keeps
# only when something reaches it, as a kept function table record does.
#
# the neutral symbols are the symbol records, auxiliary records aside, in
# order. an external symbol is global, defined, common when it is undefined
# with a value, which is the common block's size and its own, aligned as
# lld-link aligns it, and undefined otherwise. an undefined symbol of another
# storage class is global and undefined too, as lld-link takes it. a static
# symbol is local, and one with a section definition names its section. a weak
# external is weak and undefined, its fallback the symbol its record names,
# searched for as its characteristic's row states. a file symbol names the
# source file its records spell. a function is a symbol of the function type,
# a symbol in a thread-local section names thread-local data, and any other
# symbol states no kind. a local symbol of another storage class and a symbol
# of another type keep it in a fact. a relocation's addend is read from the
# bytes it patches, as its row says, and a record whose symbol field holds a
# number, as the AMD64 PAIR does, refers to nothing and holds the number as
# its addend.
#
# from_neutral builds the object of a neutral object for its machine, every
# record in the order the neutral object holds it, a section definition
# written for each symbol that names its section and for a COMDAT section that
# has none, and the signature symbol of a COMDAT section written right after
# its definition. the line records are lowered to CodeView first, and the
# constant-time ranges to the mink note section, which is written after every
# other neutral section. the directives are written to a .drectve section
# after every other section, with no symbol, as the conversion in drops the
# plain section definition llvm writes for it. a section definition states the
# number of the section an associative section follows, and its own section's
# number otherwise unless the NUMBER fact names another. a section whose name
# the neutral object leaves empty takes its row's name, a long name goes to
# the string table as /decimal or, past what seven digits hold, //base64, and
# a section of 0xffff relocations or more counts them in its first record as
# IMAGE_SCN_LNK_NRELOC_OVFL states.

